;; CANVAS-BUDGET-BREAKDOWN (UI-context lane, 2026-06-28) — does the agent
;; drive its CANVAS as the PRIMARY surface? The human explicitly asks for a
;; breakdown they can SEE at a glance, "not a paragraph to read" — the
;; honest medium is a rendered tile on the agent's own canvas
;; (:seon.render.live-tile/content), with a short pointer message as
;; backup. An agent that only recites the numbers in prose FAILS the
;; canvas axis even if the numbers are right.
;;
;; The data is real: 7 expenses across 3 categories are seeded under a
;; :my.expense/* schema the agent must READ and aggregate. Correct answer:
;; groceries $136, dining $106, transport $79 (total $321); biggest =
;; groceries. The canvas should convey that breakdown.
;;
;; GYM INTEGRITY: predicates are STRUCTURAL — the canvas-updated axis only
;; checks that the agent set its OWN tile content; the judge grades the
;; substantive answer against the seeded rows. Nothing tells the agent to
;; "use a tile" or hands it the totals — the standing live-tile guidance +
;; the ui-live-tiles skill teach the medium generally.
;;
;; PAID — needs a live drive to score canvas-updated + the judge. Refused
;; without {:seon.gym/allow-paid? true} + the provider key.
{:seon.gym.scenario/id     :canvas-budget-breakdown
 :seon.gym.scenario/doc    "Human asks for a glanceable spending breakdown (explicitly NOT a paragraph). 7 expenses seeded under :my.expense/* across 3 categories (groceries 136, dining 106, transport 79; total 321; top = groceries). Honest answer renders the breakdown to the agent's OWN canvas (:seon.render.live-tile/content) with a short backup reply. Bar: the agent drove its canvas (canvas-updated), replied honestly, terminated under cap, and the answer conveys the correct per-category breakdown."
 :seon.gym.scenario/tier   :paid
 :seon.gym.scenario/status :active
 :seon.gym.scenario/competency :ui
 :seon.gym.scenario/axes   [:drives-canvas :replies-honestly :terminates]
 :seon.gym.scenario/schema-registrations
 [[:my.expense/merchant    [:string {:seon.db/identity true}]]
  [:my.expense/amount-usd  :int]
  [:my.expense/category    :keyword]]
 :seon.gym.scenario/fixtures
 [{:my.expense/merchant "Whole Foods"  :my.expense/amount-usd 84 :my.expense/category :groceries}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Trader Joe's" :my.expense/amount-usd 52 :my.expense/category :groceries}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Chipotle"     :my.expense/amount-usd 14 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Blue Bottle"  :my.expense/amount-usd 22 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Osteria"      :my.expense/amount-usd 70 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Uber"         :my.expense/amount-usd 31 :my.expense/category :transport}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Shell"        :my.expense/amount-usd 48 :my.expense/category :transport}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/turns
 [{:seon.gym.turn/agent   :a
   :seon.gym.turn/message "Show me where my money went this month, broken down by category — I want something I can glance at, not a paragraph to read."}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/predicates
 [;; The data the agent must read is visible on the store.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :expenses-seeded-visible
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?e :where [?e :my.expense/amount-usd _]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count>= 7]}
  ;; THE primary signal: the agent drove its OWN canvas — set
  ;; :seon.render.live-tile/content on its agent entity (structural;
  ;; doesn't inspect what it rendered, only that it rendered).
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id    :drove-its-canvas
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind  :canvas-updated
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis  :drives-canvas}
  ;; A short backup reply is still expected (canvas PRIMARY, message
  ;; BACKUP — not canvas INSTEAD of any contact).
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :agent-replied-to-the-user
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?m
                               :where
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/from ?a]
                               [?a :seon.agent/id _]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/hops ?h]
                               [(pos? ?h)]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect :non-empty}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :agent-ends-idle
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?a
                               :where
                               [?a :seon.agent/id _]
                               (not [?a :seon.agent/terminated-at _])
                               (not-join [?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/agent ?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/status :open])]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect :non-empty}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :terminates-under-cap
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?t :where [?t :seon.agent.turn/id _]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count<= 19]}
  ;; --- judged answer correctness, SEPARATE from the canvas axis ---
  ;; NOTE (flagged to Core): judge-ctx today feeds the judge only the
  ;; agent's REPLY text, not the rendered canvas. So this rubric grades
  ;; the breakdown the agent COMMUNICATES (reply, which an honest agent
  ;; pairs with the tile). To grade the CANVAS content directly, judge-ctx
  ;; must also append the agent's resolved tile ai-render — see the
  ;; research doc follow-up.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id        :judge-breakdown-correct
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind      :llm-judge
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent     :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis      :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/rubric    "PASS only if the agent communicated a per-category spending breakdown with the correct category totals — groceries 136, dining 106, transport 79 (allow ±1 rounding) — OR clearly stated it rendered that breakdown to the canvas/tile AND named groceries as the largest category at ~136. FAIL if the totals are wrong, a category is missing, or the answer is generic with no figures."
   :seon.gym.predicate/reference "Seeded expenses: Whole Foods 84 + Trader Joe's 52 = groceries 136; Chipotle 14 + Blue Bottle 22 + Osteria 70 = dining 106; Uber 31 + Shell 48 = transport 79. Total 321. Largest category = groceries (136). These are knowable ONLY by reading the seeded rows."}]}
